# 112 · A research run ends when the review panel finds its questions answered

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010)

## What

A research run's minimum duration is the time it has to collect sources and claims. After it, the run checks whether its questions and hypotheses are answered. When they are, it writes its final report, with the answers, and closes itself. When they are not, it keeps researching what is missing and checks again later. The owner does not have to stop it.

Agents never judge: the workers do not decide that the research is done. Code checks the evidence first, and the supervisor's review panel decides, as it already does for a goal campaign's subjective goals.

- **When the check runs.** At a digest (every `report_cadence.digest_minutes`), once the run's running time has reached `min_duration`, when:
  - every question has at least one verified claim;
  - no review of the run is waiting for the panel;
  - the corpus changed since the run's last review (new verified claims or findings), so a review that found gaps is not asked again on the same evidence.
- **What the panel gets.** A package with the topic, each question with its verified claims (their text, sources' domains and whether they are corroborated), the run's findings, and each hypothesis with the claims cited for it. Nothing about which lane or model wrote what.
- **What each reviewer answers.** For each question: answered or not, an answer that cites verified claims, and what is missing. For each hypothesis: supported, refuted or undecided, with why and the claims it rests on.
- **What code checks in each answer.** Every cited claim is a verified claim of the run, and every number in an answer appears in the claims it cites, as for a finding. An answer that fails the check counts as not answered, with the reason.
- **The decision.** The review passes when every reviewer, at least two, finds every question answered and gives every hypothesis a verdict. A pass is accepted hands-off, unless the run asks the owner about reviews (**Ask me first about** reviews, `ask_owner.reviews`), as in goal mode.
- **On a pass:** the run lets its running trials end, writes its final report and closes with the reason `every question is answered`. The final report adds the panel's answers to each question, with the claims they cite, and its verdict on each hypothesis.
- **When the panel finds gaps:** what each reviewer said is missing goes in the run's journal and in the next workers' briefs, and the run goes on.
- **`max_duration`** still ends a run when its time is up, answered or not.
- **A rig without a review panel:** the run keeps researching, and its page says that its check waits for a review panel.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-23, about a research run 24 hours into a run with an 8-hour minimum and no maximum: "So the intent with the research harness was that the minimum time lets it grab suffecient resources and research. Then after that if it has enough data to answer the questions and hypothesis etc, then it should do that, otherwise it continues until those are suffeciently answered. I'm happy with how many claims it has. I want it to write final reports and close off cleanly without me "stopping" the run." And: "Well we have judge systems and auditors and review panels for a reason right?"

Before this goal, a research run ended only at its `max_duration` or by the owner's **Close run**. The New campaign page sets no maximum, so its research runs ran until someone closed them. A final report was the same as a digest: it had no answers.

## Done when

- [x] The harness asks for a research review at a digest after the minimum, only when the conditions above hold, and never twice on the same evidence. Tests: `src/harness/research-review.test.ts`.
- [x] The supervisor's review panel answers a research package with a research prompt and output; a supervisor from before this goal is never given one. Tests: `src/supervisor/advise-research-review.test.ts`, and `src/harness/research-review.test.ts` for `GET /v1/reviews/pending` without `kinds`.
- [x] Code checks each answer's cited claims and numbers; a pass needs every reviewer; a pass closes the run with the final report and its answers, hands-off or after the owner's acceptance when the run asks; gaps reach the journal and the workers' briefs. Tests: `src/harness/research-review.test.ts`.
- [x] The run's page and its status words say where the check stands and why the run ended. Tests: `src/control/research-check-ui.test.ts`.
- [x] The pages match the code: research mode, Why Thermite runs until the job is done, the contract reference, the review panel, Decide what waits for you, events, the glossary; the changelog.
- [ ] On the deployment, a research run past its minimum gets its review, and closes with its final report if the panel passes it.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-23, owner: build it now (the owner's words above), with the review panel deciding.
- 2026-10-23, builder, within the brief:
  - Every research run gets the check; no contract field turns it on. `max_duration` stays a hard end.
  - No new screen: the run's existing blocks and status words say where the check stands.
  - A research review is a review of the run with the reserved name `research`, so it uses the review panel's existing store and commands, including `accept_review`.
- 2026-10-23, owner (added during the build): "For the code gate we should have also a minimal floor of verified claims (Defined on the brief for a research run)." So the research contract has an optional `min_verified_claims` (a whole number from 1, no default, so older contracts keep their hash): the run must have that many verified claims, in all, before its first review. It delays the check and never ends a run. The New campaign page sets it beside **Run for at least** (**Verified claims before the check**, empty by default); Copy keeps it, as it keeps the whole contract. This replaces the earlier "no contract field" for this one floor; the check itself still needs no field.
- 2026-10-23, builder, within the What:
  - The review's evidence marker is `corpus:<verified claims>:<supported findings>:<newest verified claim>`, kept where a goal review keeps its commit, so the review table's unique index refuses a second review on the same evidence. No ledger migration.
  - The package is built when the review is asked for and kept with it. It is served, as a goal review's is, with the campaign's brief (its notes as `additional_information`), the owner's unread messages to the review panel and the run's past research. Over 200,000 characters, each question shows its corroborated claims first, then the newest, and the package says so. The reviewers also get the read-only tools that read the run's own research (goal 098).
  - A reviewer passes only when it passed the review itself and every answer and verdict holds: its own fail counts as a fail. An undecided verdict needs its why, and the claims it names must be verified claims of the run; the numbers in its why are not checked, since it asserts nothing.
  - The close is one function in the scheduler (`closeAnswered`), checked on every step with or without a model, once the run's running trials have ended: the step that adds a final writer can hook in there. The Answers and Verdicts sections are one block of the final report (`answerSections`), so a fuller paper can precede or replace it.
  - The `review_panel` event of a research review carries, for each question, how many reviewers found it answered and its first answer that passed the check (cut to 500 characters), and the gaps (each cut to 200): Needs you shows the answers before the owner accepts, and the Overview shows the gaps. `review_decided` carries the owner's note, so the hands-off words are in the event too.
  - The review panel now reads the owner's messages to it in a research run (the harness and control refused them before), since it reviews the run.
  - The workers' brief numbers questions from 0, so its gaps section does too; the journal, digests, reports and the dashboard number them from 1.
  - The shared names, the reserved review name and the close reason, are in `src/core/research-check.ts`, which the harness and control both read.

